  "description": "MAGFUX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H44 Er4 N8 O4 S4,4(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 3 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 3 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 3 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.609-3.921 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.75-114.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C48H44Er4N8O4S4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
